---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { GITHUB_URL, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import portrait from '../assets/liz-and-cat.jpg';
import birding from '../assets/about/birding.jpg';
import kestrel from '../assets/about/kestrel.jpg';
import trombone from '../assets/about/trombone.jpg';
import jerk from '../assets/about/jerk.jpg';
import squat from '../assets/about/squat.jpg';

const facts = [
	{ value: '15+', label: 'years as a software engineer' },
	{ value: '2020', label: 'first year as compiler of the Bloomington, MN CBC' },
	{ value: '1966', label: 'first year of the Bloomington count' },
	{ value: '24', label: 'count areas in the circle' },
	{ value: '2008', label: 'first year of my native plant wildlife garden' },
] as const;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="About Liz Stanley" />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<PageHero eyebrow="About" title="Hi, I'm Liz." subtitle="Software engineer, birder, Master Naturalist, photographer, and Christmas Bird Count compiler." />
		<main>
			<div class="layout">
				<div class="text">
					<p>
						I've been a software engineer for over 15 years. These days I use AI as an accelerator for
						that experience, with me in control, to write production quality applications.
					</p>
					<figure class="photo right">
						<Image src={birding} alt="Liz in a Christmas Bird Count cap with binoculars on a wooded trail" widths={[400, 800]} sizes="(max-width: 820px) 100vw, 22rem" />
						<figcaption>Birding in Panama.</figcaption>
					</figure>
					<p>
						Outside of work, most of what I build is for birds in one way or another. Since 2020 I've
						been the compiler for the{' '}
						<a href="https://www.bloomingtoncbc.org/">Bloomington, MN Christmas Bird Count</a>, which has
						run every year since 1966. Our circle has 24 count areas, so there's a lot to keep track of,
						and that's where the software comes in.
					</p>
					<p>
						It started in my own backyard. In 2008 I wanted to attract more birds, and the way to do
						that is better habitat. Most land birds feed their young insects, and native plants are what
						bring in the insects. So I started turning my half-acre suburban lot in Bloomington from turf
						grass into native plants. Over 90 species of birds have shown up since. Along the way I've
						given{' '}
						<a href="https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1uJBmMElKlyCAs47VLP4l03S_uChEig2UvJg985YbuW8/edit?usp=sharing"
							>my talk on gardening for wildlife</a
						> to a lot of groups, like Wild Ones, and in October 2021
						the City of Bloomington named me one of its Earth Action Heroes for the work.
					</p>
					<figure class="photo left">
						<Image src={kestrel} alt="Liz holding an American Kestrel on a gloved hand at Richardson Nature Center" widths={[400, 800]} sizes="(max-width: 820px) 100vw, 22rem" />
						<figcaption>Volunteering with an American Kestrel at Richardson Nature Center.</figcaption>
					</figure>
					<p>
						I'm also a Minnesota Master Naturalist. Since 2009 I've volunteered with the raptors at
						Richardson Nature Center, and I still do. I also volunteered with{' '}
						<a href="https://raptor.umn.edu/">The Raptor Center</a> for five years, and I've worked on a
						number of citizen science projects.
					</p>
					<p>
						I've had a camera on my bird feeders since 2008. The first one uploaded a still image every 30
						seconds. Today it's the{' '}
						<a href="https://feedercam.overlookcircle.org">Overlook Circle Feedercam</a>, a live stream
						that KSTP's Minnesota Live shows often, and{' '}
						<a href="https://kstp.com/special-coverage/minnesota-live/the-woman-behind-the-bloomington-bird-feeder-livestream/"
							>KSTP interviewed me</a
						> about it. I'm also a weather nerd, and I've run a Davis Vantage Pro2 weather station at
						home since 2007. Of course the two had to meet: my{' '}
						<a href="https://github.com/lizmstanley/webcam-weather">webcam-weather</a> project puts the
						live weather readings right on the video.
					</p>
					<p>
						I'm an avid photographer too. My bird photos are all of wild birds, and you can find them on{' '}
						<a href="https://pbase.com/gymell">PBase</a> and{' '}
						<a href="https://www.instagram.com/lizmstanley/">Instagram</a>. What I see goes on{' '}
						<a href="https://ebird.org/profile/MTk5Mzk1">eBird</a>.
					</p>
					<figure class="photo right tall">
						<Image src={trombone} alt="Liz holding her bass trombone" widths={[400, 800]} sizes="(max-width: 820px) 100vw, 22rem" />
						<figcaption>With my bass trombone.</figcaption>
					</figure>
					<p>
						Not everything is birds. I have two music degrees. I sang with{' '}
						<a href="https://www.thegregoriansingers.org/">The Gregorian Singers</a> and played trombone
						with the <a href="https://www.medalistband.com/">Medalist Concert Band</a> in Bloomington, and
						these days I play bass trombone with the{' '}
						<a href="https://northernwindsconcertband.org/">Northern Winds Concert Band</a>.
					</p>
					<p>
						I used to compete in weightlifting and powerlifting. I lifted with Team Spartacus and won a
						bronze medal at the 2013 Pan American Masters Championships in Chicago. On the powerlifting
						side, I set a Minnesota masters bench press record at the 2014 USAPL Minnesota Senior State
						Open (<a href="https://www.openpowerlifting.org/u/lizstanley">results</a>).
					</p>
					<div class="photo-pair">
						<figure>
							<Image src={jerk} alt="Liz holding a barbell overhead in a split jerk" widths={[400, 570]} sizes="(max-width: 820px) 50vw, 20rem" />
							<figcaption>Split jerk at a Team Spartacus meet.</figcaption>
						</figure>
						<figure>
							<Image src={squat} alt="Liz squatting a loaded barbell with spotters on each side" widths={[400, 800]} sizes="(max-width: 820px) 50vw, 20rem" />
							<figcaption>Squatting at a powerlifting meet.</figcaption>
						</figure>
					</div>
					<p>My code is on <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a>, and my <a href="/resume">resume</a> is here.</p>
				</div>
				<aside>
					<Image src={portrait} alt="Liz Stanley with her black and white cat" width={640} height={640} class="portrait" />
					<p class="eyebrow">At a glance</p>
					<dl>
						{
							facts.map((fact) => (
								<div>
									<dt>{fact.value}</dt>
									<dd>{fact.label}</dd>
								</div>
							))
						}
					</dl>
				</aside>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.layout {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 20rem;
		align-items: start;
		gap: 4rem;
	}
	.text {
		display: flow-root;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
	}
	.photo {
		width: 22rem;
		max-width: 50%;
		margin: 0.4rem 0 1.25rem;
	}
	.photo.tall {
		width: 15rem;
	}
	.photo.right {
		float: right;
		margin-left: 2rem;
	}
	.photo.left {
		float: left;
		margin-right: 2rem;
	}
	.photo img {
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		border-radius: var(--radius);
	}
	.photo-pair {
		clear: both;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 1.25rem;
		margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
	}
	.photo-pair figure {
		margin: 0;
	}
	.photo-pair img {
		width: 100%;
		height: 14rem;
		object-fit: cover;
		border-radius: var(--radius);
	}
	.photo figcaption,
	.photo-pair figcaption {
		margin-top: 0.4rem;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: var(--ink-soft);
	}
	.text p:first-child {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
	}
	aside {
		padding: 1.75rem;
		background: var(--paper-raised);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
	}
	.portrait {
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
	}
	dl {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.25rem;
		margin: 0;
	}
	dt {
		font-family: var(--font-fraunces);
		font-size: 2.2rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		line-height: 1;
		color: var(--spruce);
	}
	dd {
		margin: 0.3rem 0 0;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: var(--ink-soft);
	}
	@media (max-width: 820px) {
		.layout {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 2rem;
		}
		.photo.right,
		.photo.left {
			float: none;
			width: 100%;
			max-width: 100%;
			margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
		}
		.photo-pair img {
			height: 10rem;
		}
	}
</style>
